{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["לאסור אסר — לא יחל דברו — turns on the vow. That is, he must not delay his vow until after the festivals, as the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded, for thus it is explained: לא יחל is like ״ויחל עד בוש״, ״ויחל עוד שבעת ימים״, ״יחל ישראל אל ה׳״ — he shall wait and tarry for it. And whoever explains the language as חילול (profanation) according to the plain sense is mistaken." "ככל היוצא מפיו יעשה — turns on the oath, in the matter that he explained: בשעת שבועתו יעשה — at the time he specified for fulfillment, whether near or far. And a proof for the matter: these two things Moshe explained in Mishneh Torah: ״כי תדור נדר לה׳ אלהיך לא תאחר לשלמו״, ״מוצא שפתיך תשמור ועשית״, ״השבע שבועה וגו׳״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:02.633291674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}